  "correction_rules": [
    "Bias correction: Model consistently underestimates prices in early 30d forecasts; adjust forecast by +1.5 to +3.0 depending on recent sentiment (0.25 or above).",
    "Lag correction: Forecast often lags true price by 1–3 days; shift forecast 1–3 days forward if sentiment is neutral or positive.",
    "Overshoot after spikes: After price spikes (e.g., >65), model overcorrects downward; reduce forecast by 1.0–2.5 if spike is followed by sentiment 0.00.",
    "Mean reversion: If 30d forecast is >68 and true outcome is <66, apply downward adjustment of 1.0–3.0; if <62 and true is >64, adjust upward 1.0–2.5.",
    "Sentiment-driven horizon: If sentiment >0.25, forecast should be 1.5–2.0 higher than model; if sentiment=0.00, apply 0.5–1.0 downward bias to avoid overconfidence."
  ]
}
